<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonld={jsonld} navVariant="inner">
<section class="hero">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow">On the ground</span>
<h1>India's furniture clusters, from the inside</h1>
<p class="lead">Every cluster fails in its own way. We live in them—same-day response in Jodhpur and Jaipur, and cluster-specific risk knowledge no fly-in inspector has.</p>
<div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-independent/">Why independent</a></div>
</div>
</section>
<section><div class="wrap"><h2 class="vh">Clusters we cover</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/jodhpur/"><h3>Jodhpur — HQ</h3><p>Solid sheesham, mango, reclaimed &amp; industrial. Risks: seasoning, batch finish drift. Same-day response.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/jaipur/"><h3>Jaipur</h3><p>Carved, painted &amp; bone-inlay furniture. Risk: subcontracted carving quality. Same-day response.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/saharanpur/"><h3>Saharanpur</h3><p>Wood carving &amp; turned components. Risks: moisture and grading consistency. 48-hour response.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/moradabad/"><h3>Moradabad</h3><p>Metal &amp; metal-wood combination. Risks: weld quality, coating adhesion. 48-hour response.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/delhi-ncr/"><h3>Delhi NCR</h3><p>Upholstery, mixed-material and export houses. Risk: trader-vs-factory verification. 24-hour response.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/clusters/kolkata/"><h3>Kolkata</h3><p>Cane &amp; rattan. Risks: material treatment and mould. 72-hour response.</p></a></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><p class="prose rv">A defect is usually a cluster habit before it is a factory mistake. Jodhpur's skipped kiln cycles, Jaipur's subcontracted carving, Moradabad's coating adhesion—each has a specific inspection point that catches it. Our checklists are tuned per cluster, which is something a generalist flying in from Delhi for one day cannot offer. Proximity is also logistics: morning bookings, afternoon inspections, and re-inspections within 48 hours after rework.</p></div></section>
<section class="final">
<div class="wrap">

<h2>Your next India order. Protected.</h2>
<p>Confirmed within 2 hours. Report within 24 hours of inspection. Paid by buyers only — never by factories.</p>
<a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a>
</div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
